      "writtenOn": "2025-09-24T16:24:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It ties to CBI and its name contains a \"cbi_\" prefix. Many other similar conversions in files, for example, \"battery_\", \"typec_\", \"fp_\", and \"chipset_\", which don\u0027t contains the \"ec_\" prefix.\n\nDoes coreboot use this struct directly, or does it have its own struct for it, which would then require an \"ec_\" prefix to avoid name conflict? If the latter is the case, I can move this declaration to another EC header file.",
