      "writtenOn": "2025-09-24T16:24:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why? The UFSC fields are precisely designed not to cross a 32-bit boundary. Using a `uint32_t` reduces the complexity of parsing a field where a boundary is crossed. Since crossing an 8-bit boundary exists in some fields, special handling is needed.",
